# Chapter 5 — K8s ↔ Vault Trust Integration

## The Analogy — Same Pattern as GH ↔ AWS

Before touching any config, the mental model: this is exactly the same trust pattern as Chapter 1.

| GH ↔ AWS (Chapter 1) | K8s ↔ Vault (Chapter 5) |
|---|---|
| AWS creates OIDC provider → "I trust GitHub" | Vault enables kubernetes auth → "I trust this K8s cluster" |
| GitHub sends JWT (repo, branch, actor) | K8s pod sends JWT (service account, namespace) |
| AWS validates JWT by calling GitHub OIDC endpoint | Vault validates JWT by calling K8s TokenReview API |
| AWS checks: right repo? right branch? | Vault checks: right namespace? right service account? |
| AWS returns temporary credentials (1h) | Vault returns temporary token (configurable TTL) |
| Temp creds scoped by IAM policy | Temp token scoped by Vault policy |

Same concept, different actors. The trust is established once, then every runtime request goes through
the same handshake.

