## Vault Agent Injector — How It Actually Works

The injector is a Helm-deployed webhook running in the `vault` namespace. It watches for pods with
specific annotations and mutates them — adds an init container and a sidecar before the pod starts.

**vault-agent-init** (init container) — runs once at pod startup. Authenticates to Vault, fetches the
secret, renders it to `/vault/secrets/`. Dies after. Used for one-shot jobs like etcd-backup — pod
gets the secret at startup and that's it.

**vault-agent** (sidecar) — stays running with the pod. Authenticates, fetches, renders, then keeps
watching Vault for changes. When the secret value changes in Vault, it re-renders the file
automatically (~4.5 minutes) without restarting the pod.

The annotations that drive this:

```yaml
vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject: "true"               # enable injection
vault.hashicorp.com/role: "nginx"                      # which Vault role to use
vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject-secret-config.txt:    # what secret + where to write it
  "secret/data/nginx/config"
vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject-template-config.txt:  # how to render it (required)
  |
  {{ with secret "secret/data/nginx/config" }}
  login-password: {{ index .Data.data "login-password" }}
  {{ end }}
vault.hashicorp.com/tls-skip-verify: "false"           # enforce TLS verification
vault.hashicorp.com/tls-secret: "vault-ca"             # K8s Secret containing IPA CA cert
vault.hashicorp.com/ca-cert: "/vault/tls/ca.crt"      # path inside the sidecar
```

**Lessons learned from the injector TS case (VLT-004):**

`agent-extra-secret` is NOT the right annotation for CA certs — it mounts at `/vault/custom/`, not
`/vault/tls/`. The correct annotation is `tls-secret` which mounts at `/vault/tls/`. Spent time
figuring this out.

Without the template annotation, Vault Agent dumps the raw KV v2 API response including metadata
wrapper — not just the secret values.

Hyphenated keys in Go templates break silently. `.Data.data.login-password` is parsed as `.Data.data.login`
minus `password`. Must use `index .Data.data "login-password"`.

`{{-` trim markers inside YAML annotations conflict with the YAML parser. Remove them — use `{{` only.

Key names in the template must exactly match key names stored in Vault — a mismatch renders `<no value>`
with no error.

