## Temp Token Lifecycle and Leak Risk

Token TTL is configured in the Vault role. Default 1 hour. The token lives only inside the pod's
filesystem — never in logs, never in env vars, not visible from outside without exec access.

If the token is stolen: yes, anyone with it can read the scoped secrets until expiry. But to steal it
you need to exec into the pod or compromise the node — at which point you already have direct access to
the mounted secret files at `/vault/secrets/`. The token theft scenario doesn't give you anything you
couldn't already read directly. Theoretical risk in practice.

